Carafe bench: the arm64 backend emits an ordered load as a plain load followed by DMB ISH and an ordered store
as DMB ISH, a plain store and DMB ISH, instead of LDAR and STLR. LDAR and STLR need an aligned address on the
host, so a guest ordered access to an unaligned address raised SIGBUS and killed Eden. FEX emits such accesses
for every x86 load and store when it emulates total store ordering; on the console the access takes an
alignment fault and FEX rewrites it as a plain access with a barrier, which is what this emits.
GPL-3.0-or-later, as the file it changes.

